@prefix silm: <urn:silmaril:entity#> .
@prefix ui: <urn:silmaril:ui#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix geo: <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#> .
@prefix sf: <http://www.opengis.net/ont/sf#> .

# UI Constructor Ontology
#
# This file defines how SHACL shapes and TTL instances construct HTML/CSS.
# The ontology is not just data about the UI; it IS the UI's source of truth.
# Every HTML element, CSS property, and layout coordinate is typed here first.
#
# Key principle: The UI is a projection of the ontology, not a separate artifact.
# HTML is the render target. CSS is the style projection. RDF geometry is the
# layout authority. If the ontology cannot type a button, that button does not exist.

# === UI ELEMENT TYPES ===

ui:UIElement a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "UIElement" ;
    rdfs:comment """The root class for all user interface elements.
A UIElement is a typed projection of an ontology concept into HTML/CSS.
Every element has: a semantic type (what it means), a geometric type (where it goes),
and a style type (how it looks). No element exists without all three.""" .

ui:Container a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ui:UIElement ;
    rdfs:label "Container" ;
    rdfs:comment """A container element: div, section, article, nav, header, footer.
Containers have children and define spatial regions. Their geometry is defined
by RDF coordinate reference systems (CRS), not by CSS alone.""" .

ui:TextElement a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ui:UIElement ;
    rdfs:label "TextElement" ;
    rdfs:comment """A text-bearing element: p, h1-h6, span, code, pre.
Text elements carry lexical content. Their typography is controlled by
style properties that descend from semantic types (e.g., law-display vs.
body-text have different font families).""" .

ui:InteractiveElement a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ui:UIElement ;
    rdfs:label "InteractiveElement" ;
    rdfs:comment """An interactive element: a, button, input.
Interactive elements have behavior: href, onClick, form submission.
Their behavior is typed by the ontology, not by raw JavaScript.
Every interactive element must declare its trigger (what user action activates it),
its target (what it affects), and its precondition (what must be true for it to fire).
Without these three, the element is untyped and cannot be validated.""" .

ui:VisualElement a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ui:UIElement ;
    rdfs:label "VisualElement" ;
    rdfs:comment """A visual element: svg, img, canvas.
Visual elements display graphics. Their geometry is defined by RDF geometry
primitives (points, polygons, curves) projected through the UI CRS.
Every visual element must have a geometric type (point, line, polygon, circle)
and a style type (stroke, fill, stroke-width). Without these, the element
is not a visual element; it is an untyped blob. The ontology must be able
to render every visual element without reference to external icon libraries.""" .

# === STYLE PROPERTIES ===

ui:StyleProperty a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "StyleProperty" ;
    rdfs:comment """A CSS property defined by the ontology.
Style properties are not arbitrary CSS strings. They are typed values with
semantic meaning: --color-accent is not just a color; it is the accent color
of the Silmaril identity.""" .

ui:ColorProperty a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ui:StyleProperty ;
    rdfs:label "ColorProperty" ;
    rdfs:comment """A color property: background, text, border, accent colors.
Color is not merely aesthetic; it is semantic. The accent color of Silmaril
is not just a hex code; it is the visual signature of the identity.
Every color property must declare: its role (what it colors), its contrast
ratio against the background (for accessibility), and its semantic meaning
(what the color represents in the domain: success, failure, warning, identity).""" .

ui:TypographyProperty a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ui:StyleProperty ;
    rdfs:label "TypographyProperty" ;
    rdfs:comment """A typography property: font-family, font-size, line-height, letter-spacing.
Typography is the voice of the interface. Serif for body (authority, tradition),
monospace for code (precision, structure). Every typography property must
declare: its semantic role (body, heading, code, label), its readability
constraints (minimum size for accessibility), and its domain association
(law-display uses monospace because laws are code; body text uses serif
because narrative requires flow).""" .

ui:SpacingProperty a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ui:StyleProperty ;
    rdfs:label "SpacingProperty" ;
    rdfs:comment """A spacing property: margin, padding, gap. Values are in rem units.
Spacing is structural, not decorative. It defines relationships between
elements: proximity implies grouping, separation implies distinction.
Every spacing property must declare: its direction (top, right, bottom, left),
its scale (derived from the modular scale of the design system), and its
semantic purpose (grouping, breathing room, hierarchy). Without these,
spacing is arbitrary and the layout cannot be validated against the ontology.""" .

ui:LayoutProperty a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ui:StyleProperty ;
    rdfs:label "LayoutProperty" ;
    rdfs:comment """A layout property: display, grid-template, flex-direction.
Layout properties define how children are arranged. They are derived from
RDF geometry, not hand-written CSS. Every layout property must declare:
its structural type (grid, flex, flow), its axis (horizontal, vertical, both),
and its responsiveness (how it adapts to viewport changes). The layout is
not a CSS file; it is a geometric projection of the ontology's containment
relationships. CSS is the render target; RDF geometry is the authority.""" .

# === RDF GEOMETRY / CRS ===

ui:UICoordinateReferenceSystem a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "UICoordinateReferenceSystem" ;
    rdfs:comment """The Silmaril UI Coordinate Reference System.
A 2D coordinate system for layout: origin at top-left, X rightward, Y downward.
Units are relative: rem (root em) for scalability. The CRS is not CSS; it is
a geometric ontology that CSS projects.""" .

ui:UILayoutRegion a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "UILayoutRegion" ;
    rdfs:comment """A rectangular region in the UI CRS.
Defined by: x, y, width, height. All values are in rem units.
Regions may overlap; z-index is a separate coordinate.
Every region must be justified: why this x, why this y, why this width,
why this height. The justification references the semantic role of the
element (navigation is top because it is primary; footer is bottom because
it is terminal). Without justification, the region is arbitrary and the
ontology cannot validate the layout.""" .

ui:hasRegion a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "hasRegion" ;
    rdfs:domain ui:UIElement ;
    rdfs:range ui:UILayoutRegion ;
    rdfs:comment "Links a UI element to its geometric region in the UI CRS." .

ui:hasX a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "hasX" ;
    rdfs:domain ui:UILayoutRegion ;
    rdfs:range xsd:float ;
    rdfs:comment "X coordinate in rem units." .

ui:hasY a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "hasY" ;
    rdfs:domain ui:UILayoutRegion ;
    rdfs:range xsd:float ;
    rdfs:comment "Y coordinate in rem units." .

ui:hasWidth a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "hasWidth" ;
    rdfs:domain ui:UILayoutRegion ;
    rdfs:range xsd:float ;
    rdfs:comment "Width in rem units." .

ui:hasHeight a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "hasHeight" ;
    rdfs:domain ui:UILayoutRegion ;
    rdfs:range xsd:float ;
    rdfs:comment "Height in rem units." .

# === STYLE PROPERTY INSTANCES ===

ui:color_bg a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:ColorProperty ;
    rdfs:label "ColorBackground" ;
    rdfs:comment "Background color: warm stone." .

ui:color_text a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:ColorProperty ;
    rdfs:label "ColorText" ;
    rdfs:comment "Primary text color: dark charcoal." .

ui:color_accent a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:ColorProperty ;
    rdfs:label "ColorAccent" ;
    rdfs:comment "Accent color: muted bronze." .

ui:font_serif a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:TypographyProperty ;
    rdfs:label "FontSerif" ;
    rdfs:comment "Serif font: Source Serif 4, Georgia. For body text." .

ui:font_mono a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:TypographyProperty ;
    rdfs:label "FontMono" ;
    rdfs:comment "Monospace font: JetBrains Mono. For code, labels, navigation." .

# === ELEMENT INSTANCES: THE SILMARIL PAGE STRUCTURE ===

ui:site_nav a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:Container ;
    rdfs:label "SiteNavigation" ;
    ui:hasRegion ui:region_nav ;
    rdfs:comment "The site navigation bar. Sticky, top." .

ui:region_nav a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:UILayoutRegion ;
    ui:hasX "0.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ui:hasY "0.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ui:hasWidth "100.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ui:hasHeight "3.0"^^xsd:float .

ui:page_hero a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:Container ;
    rdfs:label "PageHero" ;
    ui:hasRegion ui:region_hero ;
    rdfs:comment "The page hero section. Title, subtitle, eyebrow." .

ui:region_hero a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:UILayoutRegion ;
    ui:hasX "0.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ui:hasY "3.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ui:hasWidth "100.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ui:hasHeight "20.0"^^xsd:float .

ui:hero_title a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:TextElement ;
    rdfs:label "HeroTitle" ;
    rdfs:comment "The main page title. Font: serif, large." .

ui:hero_subtitle a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:TextElement ;
    rdfs:label "HeroSubtitle" ;
    rdfs:comment "The subtitle below the title. Font: serif, muted." .

ui:law_display a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:TextElement ;
    rdfs:label "LawDisplay" ;
    rdfs:comment """The law display: T -> Frame(output: X, error|effect: Y).
Rendered as a centered code block. Font: mono.""" .

ui:pipeline_grid a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:Container ;
    rdfs:label "PipelineGrid" ;
    ui:hasRegion ui:region_pipeline ;
    rdfs:comment """The morphism family pipeline grid. Four cards in a 2x2 grid.
Each card is a Container with a title (TextElement) and steps (TextElement list).""" .

ui:region_pipeline a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:UILayoutRegion ;
    ui:hasX "0.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ui:hasY "23.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ui:hasWidth "100.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ui:hasHeight "40.0"^^xsd:float .

# === BUILD STATUS NOTIFICATION ===
# Runner notifications: build failures, success, warnings.
# Each status is a typed UI element, not a defaulted icon.

ui:BuildStatus a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ui:VisualElement ;
    rdfs:label "BuildStatus" ;
    rdfs:comment """A build status indicator. Not a defaulted icon.
The status is constructed from the ontology: red for fail, green for pass,
yellow for warn. The geometry is an RDF polygon (a checkmark, an X, or a triangle).
The color is derived from the semantic type (BuildStatusFail, BuildStatusPass,
BuildStatusWarn), not from a CSS class name.""" .

ui:BuildStatusPass a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ui:BuildStatus ;
    rdfs:label "BuildStatusPass" ;
    rdfs:comment """Green checkmark. All gates passed.
The pass status is not a green circle from an icon library; it is a polygon
defined by RDF geometry (a polyline forming a checkmark), colored by semantic
type (success is green because growth, life, continuation), and sized by
the modular scale. The checkmark points from left to right because progress
is left-to-right in the Latin writing system. Every property is justified.""" .

ui:BuildStatusFail a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ui:BuildStatus ;
    rdfs:label "BuildStatusFail" ;
    rdfs:comment """Red X. At least one gate failed.
The fail status is not a red circle with a line; it is two perpendicular
lines crossing, defined by RDF line geometry, colored by semantic type
(failure is red because danger, stop, correction required), and sized by
the modular scale. The X is symmetric because failure is undirected: it
points at everything that is wrong, not at a specific direction.""" .

ui:BuildStatusWarn a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ui:BuildStatus ;
    rdfs:label "BuildStatusWarn" ;
    rdfs:comment """Yellow triangle. Advisory only; not blocking.
The warning status is not a yellow triangle with an exclamation mark from
an icon library; it is a triangle (the minimal polygon) with a vertical
line and a dot, defined by RDF geometry, colored by semantic type (warning
is yellow because caution, attention, not yet danger), and sized by the
modular scale. The triangle points upward because warnings point at the
future: what will happen if you do not act.""" .

ui:build_status_ontology a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:BuildStatusPass ;
    rdfs:label "OntologyBuildPass" ;
    rdfs:comment "Ontology consolidation and validation passed." .

ui:build_status_provenance a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:BuildStatusPass ;
    rdfs:comment "Trust manifest and commit policy passed." .

ui:build_status_scripts a owl:NamedIndividual, ui:BuildStatusWarn ;
    rdfs:label "ScriptsBuildWarn" ;
    rdfs:comment "Script tests advisory; pre-existing red migration census." .
